  "review": {
    "entityID": "place:samaria_1022",
    "book": "1KI",
    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "1KI 13:32",
        "textualBasisJa": "For the saying which he cried by the LORD’s word against the altar in Bethel, and against all the houses of the high places which are in the cities of Samaria, will surely happen.”",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "cab118598506f512da600b9a12313726fd2db0164c088870a92b4612406e463c",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/1KI13.htm#V32"
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 16:24",
        "textualBasisJa": "He bought the hill Samaria of Shemer for two talents of silver; and he built on the hill, and called the name of the city which he built, Samaria, after the name of Shemer, the owner of the hill.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "749c8a0142d5f066fcb8ee79d2de3edfa01744af27ebd7d0b8fb3de83c035b96",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/1KI16.htm#V24"
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 16:28",
        "textualBasisJa": "So Omri slept with his fathers, and was buried in Samaria; and Ahab his son reigned in his place.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "0b31c0ba93de509b3f80c1ac82b27a998bb2ee5ce0a88183378e0a4e213ba5cf",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/1KI16.htm#V28"
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 16:29",
        "textualBasisJa": "In the thirty-eighth year of Asa king of Judah, Ahab the son of Omri began to reign over Israel. Ahab the son of Omri reigned over Israel in Samaria twenty-two years.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "3b1a8cb166804b7c4d83a6b710a8da7f849449fda3deacf6bf44b304cc543b7a",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/1KI16.htm#V29"
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 16:32",
        "textualBasisJa": "He raised up an altar for Baal in the house of Baal, which he had built in Samaria.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "2ee82c8e2f0cd8aec2db1910c002fc7f724c49aabe45332e3bf334858caf360e",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/1KI16.htm#V32"
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 18:2",
        "textualBasisJa": "Elijah went to show himself to Ahab. The famine was severe in Samaria.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "97dc7cbc8f289c3e15cc995ddc10fee090aaf33badefea1abb44795fc5186495",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/1KI18.htm#V2"
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 20:1",
        "textualBasisJa": "Ben Hadad the king of Syria gathered all his army together; and there were thirty-two kings with him, with horses and chariots. He went up and besieged Samaria, and fought against it.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "cb1578e6336bf961b4ae11f1e9863257b2b01b1548b19988867f2cfccebbe041",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/1KI20.htm#V1"
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 20:10",
        "textualBasisJa": "Ben Hadad sent to him, and said, “The gods do so to me, and more also, if the dust of Samaria will be enough for handfuls for all the people who follow me.”",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "7b373053b6a26f0f52413fcd3352676082d5eed47285941ec4564b8ed15fe431",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/1KI20.htm#V10"
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 20:17",
        "textualBasisJa": "The young men of the princes of the provinces went out first; and Ben Hadad sent out, and they told him, saying, “Men are coming out from Samaria.”",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "12f9aa37697a8e317e79aed5e144f2d70cdb8a221a3696e197b835ad6e1472a8",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/1KI20.htm#V17"
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 20:34",
        "textualBasisJa": "Ben Hadad said to him, “The cities which my father took from your father I will restore. You shall make streets for yourself in Damascus, as my father made in Samaria.” “I”, said Ahab, “will let you go with this covenant.” So he made a covenant with him and let him go.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "d73859893399cef8db527565119d8212a2ee4085775eaf1acbaf5bca62626d45",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/1KI20.htm#V34"
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 20:43",
        "textualBasisJa": "The king of Israel went to his house sullen and angry, and came to Samaria.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "386c4717e28869d33edabcdb41f10be61b31b24c067d5ce416b9a3b7f5e0d00a",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/1KI20.htm#V43"
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 21:1",
        "textualBasisJa": "After these things, Naboth the Jezreelite had a vineyard which was in Jezreel, next to the palace of Ahab king of Samaria.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "2f71fe7d4f0af3f1a1c91f78d8f54d4dc5d9917056affa83d3523d3f5b019a82",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/1KI21.htm#V1"
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 21:18",
        "textualBasisJa": "“Arise, go down to meet Ahab king of Israel, who dwells in Samaria. Behold, he is in the vineyard of Naboth, where he has gone down to take possession of it.",
        "sourceTextSHA256": "46af00eac85ed86aa403a5c41400bf90d40d7db0dd6c2783b8789d65575d2939",
        "citationURL": "https://ebible.org/engwebp/1KI21.htm#V18"
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 22:10",
